# GitHub Packages credential for build platforms that have no user-level npmrc —
# Cloudflare Workers Builds, which is this project's deploy path.
#
# pnpm 11 ignores registry credentials found in a project `.npmrc` unless `npmrcAuthFile`
# names that file as trusted, because a committed file could leak a literal token to an
# attacker-controlled registry. The builder opts in through its own environment:
#
#   PNPM_CONFIG_NPMRC_AUTH_FILE = .npmrc.auth      (Workers Builds variable)
#   NODE_AUTH_TOKEN             = <PAT>            (Workers Builds secret)
#
# No secret lives here: the value is an env-var placeholder, expanded at install time from
# the encrypted build secret. Locally and in GitHub Actions this file is never read —
# `npmrcAuthFile` is unset there, and `actions/setup-node` writes its own npmrc instead.
#
# Why this is NOT in `.npmrc`: that file is distributed by `josh sync`, which strips this
# exact line (kit's OBSOLETE_NPMRC_LINES). It did so during the kit 1.52.0 upgrade and the
# deploy started failing with ERR_PNPM_FETCH_401 on the first `@joshuafolkken/*` version
# that was not already in the builder's store. Keeping the credential in a file kit does
# not manage makes the deploy independent of what a sync rewrites.
# Tracking the upstream half: https://github.com/joshuafolkken/kit/issues/759
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
